/bg/\",\"title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is\"},{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/\",\"title\":\"Chapter One: Observing the Armies on the Battlefield of Kurukṣetra\"}],\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/15/\",\"bb\":252,\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"pager\":{\"previous\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/14/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 14\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]},\"next\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/16-18/\",\"title\":\"TEXTS 16-18\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]}},\"child_items\":[{\"section\":\"devanagari\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.devanagari\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.DevanagariRecord\",\"title\":\"devanagari\",\"id\":272,\"bb\":567900,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/15/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"पाञ्चजन्यं हृषीकेशो देवदत्तं धनञ्जयः ।
पौण्ड्रं दध्मौ महाशङ्खं भीमकर्मा वृकोदरः ॥ १५ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":273,\"bb\":253,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/15/b253/\",\"body_value\":\"pāñcajanyaṁ hṛṣīkeśo
devadattaṁ dhanañ-jayaḥ
pauṇḍraṁ dadhmau mahā-śaṅkhaṁ
bhīma-karmā vṛkodaraḥ\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":274,\"bb\":254,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/15/b254/\",\"shadow_value\":\"pāñcajanyam – the conchshell named Pāñcajanya; hṛṣīka-īśaḥ – Hṛṣīkeśa (Kṛṣṇa, the Lord who directs the senses of the devotees); devadattam – the conchshell named Devadatta; dhanam-jayaḥ – Dhanañjaya (Arjuna, the winner of wealth); pauṇḍram – the conch named Pauṇḍra; dadhmau – blew; mahā-śaṅkham – the terrific conchshell; bhīma-karmā – one who performs herculean tasks; vṛka-udaraḥ – the voracious eater (Bhīma).\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"pāñcajanyam\",\"translation\":\"the conchshell named Pāñcajanya\"},{\"word\":\"hṛṣīka-īśaḥ\",\"translation\":\"Hṛṣīkeśa (Kṛṣṇa, the Lord who directs the senses of the devotees)\"},{\"word\":\"devadattam\",\"translation\":\"the conchshell named Devadatta\"},{\"word\":\"dhanam-jayaḥ\",\"translation\":\"Dhanañjaya (Arjuna, the winner of wealth)\"},{\"word\":\"pauṇḍram\",\"translation\":\"the conch named Pauṇḍra\"},{\"word\":\"dadhmau\",\"translation\":\"blew\"},{\"word\":\"mahā-śaṅkham\",\"translation\":\"the terrific conchshell\"},{\"word\":\"bhīma-karmā\",\"translation\":\"one who performs herculean tasks\"},{\"word\":\"vṛka-udaraḥ\",\"translation\":\"the voracious eater (Bhīma)\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":275,\"bb\":255,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/15/b255/\",\"body_value\":\"Lord Kṛṣṇa blew His conchshell, called Pāñcajanya; Arjuna blew his, the Devadatta; and Bhīma, the voracious eater and performer of herculean tasks, blew his terrific conchshell, called Pauṇḍra.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":276,\"bb\":256,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/15/b256/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":277,\"bb\":257,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/15/b257/\",\"body_value\":\"Arjuna is referred to as Dhanañjaya in this verse because he helped his elder brother in fetching wealth when it was required by the king to make expenditures for different sacrifices. Similarly, Bhīma is known as Vṛkodara because he could eat as voraciously as he could perform herculean tasks, such as killing the demon Hiḍimba. So the particular types of conchshell blown by the different personalities on the side of the Pāṇḍavas, beginning with the Lord’s, were all very encouraging to the fighting soldiers. On the other side there were no such credits, nor the presence of Lord Kṛṣṇa, the supreme director, nor that of the goddess of fortune. So they were predestined to lose the battle – and that was the message announced by the sounds of the conchshells.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 1.15\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 1.15\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n26:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 p